course: dictionary
lesson: 4763
title: Words built from smaller words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from two smaller words. Housekeeper is made of house and keeper, and a keeper is someone who looks after something. So a housekeeper looks after a house. Spotting the parts can help you guess a word you have not met before.
explain: Read the context: «They leave him with a porter at the station, catch a slow train home, hand Toad to his housekeeper and row back to their own cosy parlour.» The housekeeper is someone who takes Toad in at his home, so she must be the person who looks after his house. Try the meaning in the sentence: hand Toad to the person who looks after his house. It still makes sense.
explain: The next sentence adds more clues: «instructed his housekeeper to feed him, undress him, and put him to bed». Feeding, undressing and putting someone to bed are caring jobs, so a housekeeper looks after people as well as the house. In a big old house, the housekeeper is also in charge of the other servants.
fact: A housekeeper is a person whose job is to look after a house: cleaning, cooking, shopping and running things for the family.
fact: In a big old house, the housekeeper was the head servant, in charge of the other servants and the household stores.
fact: «Housekeeper» can also mean someone who is good at keeping their own home tidy and running: «She is a good housekeeper.»
fact: «Good housekeeping» means sensible care of a home or of money.
fact: Keeper means someone who looks after something, so you can often work out a word by breaking it into smaller parts.
exercise: «They leave him with a porter at the station, catch a slow train home, hand Toad to his housekeeper and row back to their own cosy parlour.» What is a housekeeper? | A kind of train | A worker who sells tickets | *A person who looks after a house | A boat for rowing
exercise: Which two smaller words make up housekeeper? | hour and keeper | *house and keeper | horse and keep | home and cook
exercise: «She is a good housekeeper.» What does this sentence mean? | She is a famous writer | *She keeps her own home tidy and running well | She has lost the keys to the house | She works as a train driver
test: In «hand Toad to his housekeeper», who is the housekeeper? | The rat who rows the boat | A train driver | Toad's brother | *The person who looks after Toad's house
test: Which phrase means sensible care of a home or of money? | slow train | cosy parlour | riverside house | *good housekeeping
exam: In «instructed his housekeeper to feed him, undress him, and put him to bed», what does the sentence show about a housekeeper's job? | *Looking after a person as well as the house | Rowing a boat | Driving a train | Only cleaning windows
